ue comments, they are never linked to the corresponding commit – whether separate on a line or enclosed by text (yes, I saw #1667), whether shortened to 7, 10 or not at all (in which case the parser *shortens the string,* but doesn't link it) – no link.\r\n\r\nOf course the corresponding commits exist in the very same project, so it's not that there'd be no target. As the linking does work on try.gitea.io it seems that either something must be missing with my installation (single-binary drop-in: `gitea-1.1.2-linux-arm-7`), or this is a bug specific to the ARM build.\r\n\r\n## Example\r\nFor this input:\r\n\r\n    foo\r\n\r\n    5c5c946673 \r\n\r\n    bar 5c5c946673ebd1fdcc996a5a198699b4e3ace9b4\r\n\r\n\r\nResult is rendered like this:\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"ui bottom attached tab segment markdown active\" data-tab=\"preview\"><p>foo</p>\r\n\r\n      <p>5c5c946673</p>\r\n\r\n      <p>bar 5c5c94667</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\nThe last line suggests Gitea *did* recognize it as hash, as otherwise I don't see why it got shortend.","closed_by":{"login":"bkcsoft","id":4726179,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjYxNzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4726179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/bkcsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://